Day 1 - Baseline + Scope Lock

Scope lock (2 weeks):
- [ ] Freeze major feature changes for 2 weeks (except critical bugs)
- [ ] Focus only on reliability, tests, performance, security, and release readiness
- [ ] Any new feature request goes to backlog (not this sprint)

KPI targets and baseline:

1) Booking success rate
- Definition: successful booking confirmations / booking checkout attempts
- Baseline (current): ___ %
- 2-week target: >= 98.0%
- Measured from: booking checkout logs + confirmed booking records

2) Payment success rate
- Definition: successful Stripe checkout completions / checkout session creations
- Baseline (current): ___ %
- 2-week target: >= 97.0%
- Measured from: Stripe webhook completed events + session creation logs

3) Refund completion rate
- Definition: successful refunds / total refunds requested
- Baseline (current): ___ %
- 2-week target: >= 99.0% within 24 hours
- Measured from: booking/refund status records (refunded vs refund_pending)

4) API p95 latency
- Definition: 95th percentile response time per endpoint
- Baseline (current):
  - GET /api/bookings/availability: ___ ms
  - POST /api/bookings/create-checkout-session: ___ ms
- 2-week target:
  - GET /api/bookings/availability: p95 < 200 ms
  - POST /api/bookings/create-checkout-session: p95 < 500 ms
- Measured from: k6 load test report + server timing logs

How to measure this week:
- [ ] Enable structured logging for booking/payment/refund events
- [ ] Run baseline k6 tests for availability + checkout session endpoints
- [ ] Capture Stripe webhook completion and refund outcomes
- [ ] Record current baseline values above

Definition of done (Day 1):
- [ ] KPI list is clear and measurable
- [ ] Baseline placeholders are ready or filled with first measured values
- [ ] Target numbers are set and realistic
- [ ] Scope lock is agreed for the next 2 weeks